Real-World Example

Suppose you upload a file named employee_data.csv.

Instead of manually preprocessing it:

The AI detects 120 missing salary values.
It decides to fill them with the median salary.
It removes 25 duplicate records.
It identifies age outliers (e.g., 150 years old) and removes them.
It converts the Department column into numerical values.
It scales the Salary column.
It validates the cleaned dataset.
It generates a preprocessing report.
The cleaned dataset is ready for machine learning.

All these decisions are made autonomously by collaborating agents.

